@startuml esb_decommission_responsibilities

title Apache Camel ESB Decomposition

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "As-Is" {
  [Apache Camel ESB] as camel
}

package "To-Be Target Architecture" {
  [API Gateway] as api
  [Event Bus] as eventbus
  [Domain Validators] as validators
  [Data Contracts] as contracts
  [Anti-Corruption Layer] as acl
  [Mapping Services] as mapping
  [Data Platform Ingestion Pipelines] as pipelines
  [Consumer Idempotency] as idempotency
  [Domain Services] as domains
  [Legacy Adapter / Strangler Layer] as legacy
}

camel --> api : sync transport
camel --> eventbus : async transport
camel --> validators : FLC
camel --> contracts : schema and contract checks
camel --> acl : legacy transformations
camel --> mapping : message mappings
camel --> pipelines : batch / stream transformations
camel --> idempotency : deduplication rules
camel --> domains : business logic
camel --> legacy : temporary legacy routes

note right of camel
Apache Camel is not replaced only by
API Gateway and Event Bus.

Transport moves to API/Event Bus.
FLC, transformations, reliability patterns
and business logic move to dedicated layers.
end note

@enduml
